All coding, documentation, and testing conventions for this repository live in AGENTS.md
at the repository root. Read AGENTS.md before making any edit.

Conventions are maintained in exactly one place so that every agent (Claude, Cursor,
Copilot, Gemini, Aider, ...) and every human contributor works from the same rules. Do not
add project conventions to this file — add them to AGENTS.md.

Two sections of AGENTS.md are worth reading twice, because breaking them fails silently:

- Section 2, "Hard rules": never commit /bot/ or mod/webhook.txt (live secrets), never
  change the JSONL schema without bumping schema_version, never weaken a lint/type/test
  gate to make it pass, always anchor .gitignore directory rules with a leading slash.

- Section 7, "Cross-component invariants": /rl/src/herbert_rl/policy/backbone.py must stay
  an architectural mirror of /nn's model modules or checkpoint weights are silently
  dropped; several files in /rl are deliberate hand-synced copies of /nn equivalents;
  _TARGET_KEYS is duplicated in two /nn modules; changing the per-tick tensor layout
  requires bumping feature_schema_version in nn/src/herbert_nn/data/config.py.

When creating a pull request, add this footer at the very end of the PR body:

```
Generated by cursor
```
